{# === EmptyAltRule fixture =============================================
Verifies AST-aware detection of `alt: ''` hash entries. Replaces the
Python `empty-alt` regex.

`alt: ''` is the convention for decorative images, but it is also the
easiest accessibility mistake to make on a content image. The rule
fires on every empty literal so the developer confirms the intent.

Skip conditions inherited from the Python regex:
- non-`alt` keys (any other hash field) — skipped
- non-string values (variables, function calls, concat) — skipped
- non-empty alt strings (real descriptions) — skipped

Note: the double-quoted variant (`alt: ""`) would also fire the rule, but
the project's SingleQuoteRule rejects double-quoted strings before this rule
can even run, so a dedicated test case for that path stays out of the fixture.

Run from repo root:

vendor/bin/twig-cs-fixer lint --config tests/config/twig-wordpress.php tests/Fixtures/Twig/empty-alt-fixture.twig

Expected: 4 warnings, 0 errors (EmptyAlt) — sections 1, 4, 6, 8
====================================================================== #}

{# 1) FAIL: bare empty single-quoted alt #}
{% set image1 = { src: 'foo.jpg', alt: '' } %}

{# 2) OK: alt with a real description #}
{% set image2 = { src: 'foo.jpg', alt: 'A red car parked on a sunny street' } %}

{# 3) OK: alt comes from a variable — assume intentional #}
{% set image3 = { src: 'baz.jpg', alt: my_alt } %}

{# 4) FAIL: empty alt inside an inline component call #}
{{ component_picture({ src: templateUrl ~ '/images/x.jpg', alt: '' }) }}

{# 5) OK: same call with descriptive alt #}
{{ component_picture({ src: templateUrl ~ '/images/x.jpg', alt: 'Team photo at conference' }) }}

{# 6) FAIL: empty alt inside a list of image objects #}
{% set gallery = [
	{ src: 'g1.jpg', alt: '' },
	{ src: 'g2.jpg', alt: 'Sunset over the ocean' },
] %}

{# 7) OK: non-`alt` key with empty string — rule scope is `alt` only #}
{% set link = { href: '/about', title: '' } %}

{# 8) FAIL: nested hash deeper in a structure #}
{% set hero = {
	background: {
		image: { src: templateUrl ~ '/images/hero-bg.jpg', alt: '' },
	},
} %}

{# 9) OK: alt value comes from a function call — skipped #}
{% set image9 = { src: 'foo.jpg', alt: get_alt_text('hero') } %}

{# 10) OK: alt is the result of concatenation — skipped (BinaryConcat, not ConstantExpression) #}
{% set image10 = { src: 'foo.jpg', alt: 'Image of ' ~ content.name } %}

{# 11) OK: pattern lives inside a Twig comment — comment text isn't parsed as ArrayExpression #}
{# example: { alt: '' } — bad pattern, but commented out #}
